            <ArticleTitle>Versatile (η6-arene)Ni(PCy3) nickel monophosphine precursors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13176-13179</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc08416a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nickel monophosphine arene adducts have been proposed as highly reactive intermediates capable of difficult C-O bond activation steps in Ni catalyzed cross-coupling reactions. The addition of N-methylmorpholine N-oxide to arene solutions of ([Cy3P)2Ni]2N2 allows for the synthesis of stable (η6-arene)Ni(PCy3) complexes. The isolation of these species demonstrates their viability as intermediates and provides an experimental means to test the hypothesized importance of the Ni(PCy3) moiety in bond activation and catalysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
